	abstract = {As of the rapid growth of IoT, main characteristics like large-scale deployment, dynamic topology, resource constraints, and significant security issues have been introduced. According to recent research, the traditional security measures are ineffective when it comes to dealing with such issues; that is because of the different nature of IoT. On the other hand, blockchain technology has shown a promising paradigm, as it offers distributed and decentralized security for real-time data. In this paper, a novel IoT-blockchain security framework that aims to ensure data integrity and tamper-proof logging for IoT-generated data has been introduced. The framework attempts to integrate lightweight blockchain mechanisms with off-chain storage and smart contract-based access policies so as to enable scalable, secure, and auditable data management. Unlike existing solutions, the proposed framework combines edge-based lightweight cryptographic processing with cloud-hosted blockchain nodes so as to balance security and resource efficiency. The proposed framework has been implemented on a Raspberry Pi edge gateway, and its performance was evaluated in terms of latency, throughput, resource usage, and security resilience. The achieved results show 99% data integrity verification accuracy, with an acceptable latency overhead for the non-real-time IoT applications. This work highlights the feasibility of secure, scalable IoT data management for smart city and industrial IoT scenarios. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
	author_keywords = {Blockchain; Cloud; IoT; Security framework},
