	abstract = {In today's digital era, vast amounts of data are stored using cloud services provided by various companies. To make sure the security and wholeness of this data, external auditors known as third-party auditors (TPAs) utilize cryptographic techniques for verification. The main focus of these auditing methods is to uphold privacy and enhance security within the realm of cloud data storage. The goal is to create a reliable resource that can be accessed as needed, reducing the need for continuous online data retrieval. Cloud storage plays a pivotal role in securely housing information within a network of interconnected computers. In this environment, data is stored, and applications are executed on cloud platforms. The benefits of cloud computing are numerous, including easy access to user files and documents from any location globally, cost savings, scalability, and ample storage capacity. Nevertheless, a significant challenge in the field of cloud computing revolves around establishing robust security measures. Key elements associated with this context include blockchain, compound cloud, public and private cloud.  Β© 2025 Author(s).},
