	affiliations = {Dayananda Sagar College of Engineering, Department of Computer Science, Bengaluru, India},
	abstract = {Decentralized Finance (DeFi) leverages blockchain technology to securely manage financial transactions, ensuring transparency, reliability, and trust within digital ecosystems. Platforms such as Ethereum have demonstrated remarkable growth and widespread adoption, highlighting the potential of blockchain in transforming the financial sector. Despite these advancements, early DeFi systems faced significant challenges, particularly user concerns regarding data security, transaction integrity, and overall system reliability. The research focuses on enhancing the security of DeFi transactions by utilizing blockchain's cryptographic mechanisms to safeguard sensitive financial information from unauthorized access, tampering, or fraud. The research demonstrate, a financial web application was developed using a custom blockchain server that integrates the Data Encryption Standard (DES) for encryption and decryption, along with the Secure Hash Algorithm (SHA256) to ensure data integrity. The application facilitates secure token-based exchanges for loan approvals, providing a practical implementation of secure DeFi operations. The results show that the proposed system ensures secure, tamperresistant financial exchanges. Experimental findings further confirm improvements in confidentiality, auditability, and overall reliability of decentralized transactions. The work contributes to the integration of strong cryptographic protocols within a DeFi-based loan approval model, thereby strengthening security measures, promoting safer financial operations, and enhancing user confidence in decentralized financial systems. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
