	abstract = {This project explores how we can create electronic voting systems that are secure, transparent, and efficient by leveraging blockchain technology, especially on the Ethereum platform. Traditional voting mechanisms are often plagued by inefficiencies, susceptibility to fraud, and a lack of transparency. Additionally, many existing e-voting solutions suffer from centralization and inherent security flaws. In contrast, blockchain technology provides a decentralized, immutable, and cryptographically secure framework for the storage and processing of votes. The study incorporates advanced cryptographic methodologies, such as SHA-256 hashing, elliptic curve digital signatures, and zero-knowledge proofs, to ensure voter anonymity, maintain data integrity, and facilitate secure transaction processing. A smart contract-driven architecture is employed to automate and validate crucial electoral processes, including voter registration, vote casting, and tallying. By decentralizing these functions, the system mitigates single points of failure and enhances transparency, allowing for public auditability of the election process while preserving voter privacy.This research advances the field of blockchain-based e-voting by tackling challenges related to scalability, user inclusiveness, and adherence to legal frameworks, thereby presenting a viable solution for contemporary democratic practices.  Β© 2025 IEEE.},
