	abstract = {The swift increase in the digital data sharing has compounded the necessity of the safety of secure, decentralized and tamper resistant file sharing mechanisms. Traditional centralized networks are extremely susceptible to failure points, data breaches and censorship, which are not reliable over time. In order to overcome these issues, the paper proposes Data Share, a decentralized system that combines the blockchain system with the InterPlanetary File System and Advanced Encryption Standard encryption. Typically, blockchain is used in this architecture as an unchangeable registry of cryptographic hashes and metadata and IPFS as scalable peer-peer file storage, which results in a minimal load on the on-chain data. AES encryption provides confidentiality between the files and the user controls their cryptographic keys. Experimental analysis shows that the system can decrease blockchain storage by 8590% of the time compared to storing the entire files, and maintain integrity, immutability, and auditability. Performance testing also shows that encryption and hashing have few computational overheads, which verify the scalability. In that way, Data Share is an efficient, secure, and practical way of decentralized file management. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
