	abstract = {Federated Learning empowered Digital Twins may potentially provide a high-fidelity, privacy-preserving vision of distributed assets. However, verifiable trust, auditability, and interpretability at scale are difficult. This article presents ChainFedTwin, a seven-layered framework that tightly integrates federated learning with blockchain-supported governance and a multi-modal Explainable-AI layer. ChainFedTwin improves current DT frameworks by proposing advanced cryptographic methods, safe bias detection and protection mechanisms, and smart contract-based governance to realize security, privacy, and fairness upgrades. The XAI layer integrates SHAP and LIME for end-to-end interpretability and contains embedded bias detection per aggregation step with fairness validation services. Experimental evaluation on the NSL-KDD dataset proves that ChainFedTwin outperforms the baseline FedAvg algorithm substantially. Specifically, ChainFedtwin achieved a final test accuracy of 94.1% while FedAvg was 91%, an improvement of 3.1 percentage points. Apart from that, it converged to 90% accuracy in 48 iterations, a 47% iteration decrease from FedAvg's 91 iterations, reflecting enhanced convergence speed and stability at the lower end final loss. While it causes about a 15% communication overhead due to privacy and auditing requirements, this is an acceptable compromise for increased security, trustworthiness, and interpretability in mission-critical DT applications. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
