	abstract = {With the progress of smart transport and vehicular networks, protecting data privacy and the security of user communication has become increasingly important. This paper presents a fresh approach to a blockchain-based architecture which maintains the privacy of vehicle users when interacting with smart applications. Current vehicular networks have serious limitations around centralized data and management approaches: they are prone to data tampering and unauthorized access. The method presented in this study combines decentralized records and cryptographic tools to store sensitive user data so that the data is protected while enabling access control and authentication. Smart contracts are used to automate transaction validation against intended privacy policies without Transactional intermediaries. The system architecture facilitates anonymized vehicular data access to only authorized users, which will help mitigate the opportunities for identity exposure and abuse of data. The verification method proposed is shown here to have low latency, to be scalable, and trustworthy; regardless of a reasonably common threat through a network attack. The experimental analysis shows the method presented can be trustworthy, achieve data integrity, data privacy, and access that can be trusted in real time. This method is a potential step towards building smart transport systems that open up the potential of multi-hop vehicular networks through blockchain technology.  Β© 2025 IEEE.},
