	abstract = {This paper addresses the deficiencies in traditional bid evaluation expert selection, such as low semantic accuracy and a lack of verifiable credibility. We design an intelligent system that integrates the Sentence-BERT (SBERT) model with blockchain technology to overcome these challenges. The core of the system employs the SBERT model to semantically map project requirements and expert profiles into a unified vector space. This enables similarity-based matching and ranking, moving beyond keyword-based methods and significantly improving selection accuracy. To establish trust, the system implements a blockchain-based evidence mechanism. This mechanism leverages national cryptographic algorithms (SM2, SM4) for security, recording critical selection data and result hashes as immutable transactions. This ensures full auditability and traceability, effectively mitigating integrity risks and providing technical self-certification for the process's fairness. The system has been successfully deployed in a railway bureau. The intelligent module demonstrates markedly higher matching accuracy and efficiency than conventional methods, while the blockchain component substantially elevates procedural credibility. This work thus presents a practical, trustworthy, and intelligent model for expert selection in high-stakes domains. Β© 2025 IEEE.},
