	affiliations = {Dept.of IT, SNIST, India; Dept.of IT, SNIST, India},
	abstract = {In today's dynamic landscape of smart grid technologies, the assurance of secure and transparent energy transactions stands as a critical imperative for the efficient optimization of energy distribution and consumption. This paper introduces an innovative blockchain based methodology designed specifically for meter reading within smart grid systems. By harnessing the capabilities of RSA cryptography and proof of work (PoW) mechanisms, the proposed system aims to significantly enhance data integrity and foster trust among all stakeholders involved. At its core, the system facilitates secure meter reading transactions between electricity producers and consumers, while concurrently ensuring the integrity and immutability of data storage. By leveraging blockchain technology, the system establishes tamper resistant data storage and enables the creation of transparent audit trails, essential for maintaining accountability and trustworthiness throughout the energy transaction process. Key functionalities of the system encompass the generation of cryptographic keys tailored for both producers and consumers. These keys play a pivotal role in ensuring the authenticity and confidentiality of meter reading transactions. Additionally, the system employs digital signatures to validate meter reading transactions, thus further fortifying the integrity and security of the data exchanged between parties. A cornerstone feature of the proposed system lies in its utilization of PoW consensus mechanisms for transaction validation. Through rigorous experimentation and validation processes, the system demonstrates resilience against potential tampering attempts, ensuring the integrity and accuracy of meter readings. Furthermore, the system offers real time visibility into energy consumption patterns, empowering stakeholders with actionable insights to optimize energy management strategies. Crucially, the system's adherence to industry standards and protocols ensures interoperability and regulatory compliance, thereby facilitating seamless integration within existing smart grid infrastructures. By embracing blockchain technology, the findings of this research underscore its transformative potential in revolutionizing energy transactions within smart grid environments. Ultimately, this innovation paves the way for a sustainable and resilient energy future, characterized by heightened efficiency, transparency and trust. Β© Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.},
