	abstract = {Blockchain, a distributed ledger that stores data in records (blocks) that are securely connected to one another using cryptographic hashes. Each block has a cryptographic hash of the preceding block, timestamp, and transaction data. It is tamper-proof, secure, transparent, immutable, and robust. Storing data on multiple blockchains provides a distributed solution, easing scalability concerns through parallel processing and reduced strain on any single network. Cross-chain technology enhances interaction between blockchains, fostering a more interconnected decentralized ecosystem and improving scalability. The use of a Decentralized Chameleon Hash Function for data updates ensures secure and verifiable modifications, addressing immutability concerns and maintaining blockchain integrity. But this leads to face a difficult task, to guarantee the consistency of data updates in cross-chain. This work ensures the consistency of data updating between blockchains in a decentralized way. It includes smart contracts, and Cross-chain transmissions and protocols like Cosi Protocol SHA-256 and POW to solve the consistency issues. Β© 2025 American Institute of Physics Inc.. All rights reserved.},
