	affiliations = {Dept. of IT, Sreenidhi Institute of Science and Technology, India; Dept. of IT, Sreenidhi Institute of Science and Technology, India},
	abstract = {Ensuring the integrity, security, and transparency of digital evidence is a critical challenge in modern forensic investigations. This research proposes a decentralized Blockchain-based Evidence Management System (BEMS) to establish an immutable, tamper-proof, and auditable framework for handling forensic evidence. The system leverages a permissioned blockchain architecture with smart contracts to automate evidence tracking, ownership verification, and access control. Cryptographic hashing ensures data immutability, while zero- knowledge proofs (ZKP) and homomorphic encryption enhance privacy and confidentiality. A consensus mechanism, optimized for forensic chain-of-custody requirements, ensures secure validation of transactions while maintaining computational efficiency. The proposed model is evaluated against conventional centralized evidence management systems, demonstrating superior resistance to data tampering, unauthorized access, and single points of failure. Performance metrics, including latency, throughput, and security resilience, validate the effectiveness of the blockchain-powered system in real-world forensic applications. The study further explores off-chain storage solutions to manage large-scale digital evidence efficiently while maintaining blockchain integrity. This research advances forensic science by introducing a high-assurance, transparent, and decentralized digital evidence management framework, paving the way for next-generation cybersecurity and legal compliance solutions. Future work will integrate Artificial Intelligence (AI)-driven anomaly detection to further enhance the security and efficiency of forensic investigations. Β© Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.},
